# D Tool — optional environment variables. Nothing here is required to run.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development, or set the same names in your host's
# dashboard (Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube on a host YouTube does not trust
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube scores the IP address a request comes from. Every serverless host is a
# datacenter address, so a deployment can be bot-challenged ("Sign in to confirm
# you're not a bot" → HTTP 503 from /api/fetch) while the same code works fine
# from a home connection. Check what your deployment actually sees first:
#
#   curl -s https://<your-app>/api/youtube?id=dQw4w9WgXcQ
#
# Then reach for these in order — each is more effort and more reliable than the
# one above it. None of them is needed on a host YouTube already trusts.

# 1. A visitor id minted on a network YouTube trusts. Cheapest fix, no account.
#    Get one by running this on a normal home connection:
#      curl -s -X POST 'https://www.youtube.com/youtubei/v1/visitor_id?prettyPrint=false' \
#        -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#        -d '{"context":{"client":{"clientName":"WEB","clientVersion":"2.20240726.00.00"}}}'
# YT_VISITOR_DATA=

# 2. A signed-in cookie header, copied from a browser on youtube.com (DevTools →
#    Network → any request → Request Headers → Cookie). Reliable, but it ties
#    every download to that account — use a throwaway one, never your main.
# YT_COOKIE=

# 3. An HTTP(S) proxy for youtube.com and googlevideo.com traffic only. The most
#    reliable fix, and the only one that also moves the media reads off the
#    host's address. Any proxy URL undici accepts works.
# YT_PROXY=http://user:pass@host:port

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries — resolved automatically, override only if you must
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FFMPEG_PATH=      # used ahead of the bundled ffmpeg-static binary
# YTDLP_PATH=       # optional fallback engine, absent by default
# PYTHON_PATH=      # interpreter for `python -m yt_dlp`

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com   # canonical URLs, sitemap, robots
